  "result": "I fixed the bug that let the last owner be removed. The member-service tests pass (6/6), including the one that refuses to remove the last remaining owner. I haven't run the full test suite or a type-check.\n\n**Cause:** `removeMember` in `src/server/services/member-service.ts` ran the owner check with `\"owner\"` as the member's next role. The check (`assertLastOwnerRetained`) exits immediately when the next role is `\"owner\"`, because staying an owner can never leave the org without one. So on removal it never counted the remaining owners. Demotion wasn't affected because it passes the real new role, which is why that was still refused.\n\n**Fix:**\n- `assertLastOwnerRetained` now accepts `null` as the next role, meaning \"being removed\".\n- `removeMember` passes `null` instead of `\"owner\"`, so removal goes through the same owner count as demotion.\n- I updated the function's signature in `scripts/manifest-parts/server.ts` to match.",
